/// The entities in a level that Calcite runs, item entities, experience orbs, armor stands, mobs
/// and arrows (CAL-148, CAL-154, CAL-155, CAL-156, CAL-159), as vanilla's
/// `PersistentEntitySectionManager` and `EntityTickList` keep them: in the order they came, the
/// order they tick in, and by the section each is in, in the order each came into it, so `find` and
/// its kin give them in the order `EntitySectionStorage.getEntities` does, section by section. One
/// that goes is out of both at once, so nothing after finds it, and its ID is kept for its trackers
/// to tell.
///
/// Each tick, `tick` runs each there was as it began whose chunk is in range to tick its
/// entities, as `ServerLevel.tick` runs the tick list: an item's tick to where it merges, then its
/// merging with the items near it, `mergeWithNeighbours`, then the rest; an orb's to where it looks
/// for orbs to take in, `scanForMerges`, then that, then the rest; an armor stand's and a mob's,
/// what it shows besides its sounds kept with its ID for the server to send among them, a mob's
/// after its look at whether it goes, `checkDespawn`, which may take it, and before its pushes,
/// `pushEntities`, of the mobs and players it meets (CAL-156); an arrow's to its steps along its
/// way, then those, each stopped at the entities it hits for its level to deal the hits, then the
/// rest (CAL-159). One that comes during a tick first
/// ticks the next. The players of the level are in the same list, so the server ticks these
/// one at a time, `tick_next`, those that came before each player first. Vanilla's list holds only
/// the entities of chunks that tick them, adding a chunk's in its sections' order as it comes to
/// tick them, where Calcite's keeps every one in the order it came and passes over those that
/// don't tick.
///
/// A chunk's entities are saved in its sections' order, `in_chunk`, as `storeChunkSections` saves
/// them (CAL-148). The entities read that Calcite doesn't have yet have places in the sections
/// too, by IDs below 0 the caller gives them, `place_kept`, so they're saved among the rest in the
/// order they came into each, though nothing finds or ticks them.
module world.entities

import math.mth.{floor}
import nbt.tag.{Tag}
import random.taped.{TapedRandom}
import registry.components.{ItemCodecs}
import world.arrow.{Arrow, OwnerView, Target}
